# tc_sram_xilinx writes only the first byte

The signal `be_al` and `we_al` being only one bit wide only the first byte of a word is written on FPGA. See fix proposed in PR https://github.com/pulp-platform/tech_cells_generic/pull/30














PR title: tc_sram_xilinx: Re-align be_al signal

PR description:
"The be_al signal is only one bit wide which causes to write only the first byte of the dataword on the safety island on Carfield FPGA." The PR proposed a fix that was undergoing testing on the Carfield hardware platform.

